    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1432">

                <pb facs="0940" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/369.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul General Hanna.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 16, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Spanish Ambassador informs the Department that he has received information that
                    Constitutionalists at Zacatecas have shot three priests and expelled about
                    twenty and that several sisters of Saint Therese of whom some are Spanish are in
                    hiding at that place.</p>
                <p>Bring to attention of Carranza with renewed suggestion as to advisability of
                    moderate and kind treatment of persons connected with religious
                    organizations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
